From 316fec45e3fe140dae4edee9f0d8f5c24e848e21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 23:10:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02208/11362] [outer-loop] value/novelty-guided explorer v3
 (deep tail); wa30 resists -> needs value-transfer

graph_explore_solve_v3: best-first by optional verifier (predicted steps-to-go, learned
verifier feeds back) else count-based novelty + depth bias, frame-change-only transitions
-- for deep/sparse games. wa30 (~33-deep keyboard) still no-advance @25k exp: the hard
tail needs per-game RE OR a transferred verifier (cross-game value transfer = next build;
v3 accepts it). Net: stronger explorer solves r11l + ls20 adapter-free (was 0); wa30 is
the SOTA-consistent hard tail (median 30/52).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
